<DocsLayout
  title="Installation"
  description="How to download, install and launch Mockingbird on Windows and Linux (x86_64)."
  jsonLd={howToLd}
  locale="en"
>
  <h1>Installation</h1>
  <p>
    Mockingbird is a PySide6 desktop app for Windows 10/11 and Linux (x86_64).
    Download the build for your OS from the
    <a href="https://github.com/Mockingbird-go-on/mockingbird/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">releases page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Windows</strong> 10/11 or <strong>Linux</strong> (x86_64).</li>
    <li>NVIDIA GPU with CUDA — to accelerate speech recognition (optional, but recommended).</li>
    <li>~2–4 GB of disk space for the <code>faster-whisper large-v3-turbo</code> model.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="windows">Windows</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Download <code>Mockingbird-setup.exe</code> from the latest release.</li>
    <li>Run the installer and follow the wizard steps.</li>
    <li>Launch the app from the Start menu.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    If CUDA is not detected, the app automatically falls back to CPU — recognition
    still works, just slower.
  </p>

  <h2 id="linux">Linux</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Download <code>Mockingbird.AppImage</code>.</li>
    <li>Make the file executable and run it:</li>
  </ol>
  <pre><code>chmod +x Mockingbird.AppImage
./Mockingbird.AppImage</code></pre>

  <h2 id="first-launch">First launch</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Check the device indicator in the toolbar: <code>GPU</code> or <code>CPU</code>.</li>
    <li>Upload a PDF résumé on the <strong>Résumé</strong> tab (optional).</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Start</strong> and speak — the draft appears on the <strong>Interview</strong> tab.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Updating</h2>
  <p>
    The app checks for new releases on startup. Manually — on the
    <a href="https://github.com/Mockingbird-go-on/mockingbird/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">releases page</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Next: <a href="/docs/en/setup/stt-model/">choosing an STT model</a> and
    <a href="/docs/en/setup/modes/">operating modes</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
